{"t": 1784297359.682, "run_id": "fc_sphinx_repo_s1_20260717_070126", "kind": "swe_task", "tag": "frozenmem", "idx": 5, "instance": "sphinx-doc__sphinx-9320", "scope": "repo:sphinx-doc/sphinx", "nc": 1, "n": 1, "exit_statuses": ["Submitted"], "judge": [{"success": true, "verified": true, "reason": "The patch correctly fixes the root cause of the issue. The problem was that when `sphinx-quickstart` encounters an existing `conf.py`, it prompts the user to enter a new root path with the message 'or just Enter to exit'. However, the validator used (`is_path`) rejected empty strings, preventing users from exiting. The fix introduces a new `is_path_or_empty` validator that allows empty strings (to trigger exit) while still validating non-empty paths. The code correctly checks `if not d['path']: sys.exit(1)` to handle the empty string case."}], "n_retrieved": 4, "ret_scores": [0.73, 0.702, 0.7, 0.699], "mem_chars": 2514, "n_memory": 68}
